# Gap analysis — spec 0042

> This is the "what's missing / what drifted" companion to `.summary-md` (the
> narrative) and `.stat-md` (the numbers). It is not a substitute for either.

**Scope.** Two passes. Pass 1 compares the operator's preliminary spec —
`.manual/004-mueller-inverse-reconstruction-test.md`, named as the preliminary in
`.history` and superseding the `002` draft (it folds in the `003-comments.txt`
answers) — against the authored `.spec-md` / `.spec-jsonl`. Pass 2 compares the
authored spec's commitments against what actually landed in the tree.

Pass 1 is a **high-fidelity transfer**: all 26 functions named in the
preliminary's §5.4 inventory appear in the jsonl steps, as do all four pure unit
tests from §5.6, all four per-family gain rules from §3, and every §4 target
number that §5.6 put in core scope. The preliminary's own §5.6 future-candidate
list maps 1:1 onto `.spec-md` §0's named-exclusion list. The gaps below are, with
one exception, small.

